Z||000000||fiero56||01-28-2000||11:36 AM||||I just picked up the flywheel today from the dealer. With tax it came out to $250 and change. It came in a cardborad box/sleeve and is a litte dirty, but new. Is there anything I should use to clean it up before I install it. Will brake cleaner work? I don't want anyone(me) to have to dig down in the engine again for another 150,000 miles. Is there any prep I should do to the flywheel/clutchset?||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||01-28-2000||12:55 PM||||Wow, I hadn't realized that they had gotten so expensive, was that through the dealer? Brake clean and a clean rag should be fine.||||reg||3
Z||000002||theogre||01-28-2000||07:31 PM||||clean it, install it, then clean the face again before putting the disk to it. clean the pressure plate face as well. Don't let cleaner get to the back of the presure plate and wash out any lubricants.<P>brake cleaner is fine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||01-28-2000||09:05 PM||||Thanks guys, I used brake cleaner last time, and didn't know if that would have helped cause this problem or not. Ogre, just wondering, what happens if you get cleaner on the back of the face of the plate. Don't worry, I haven't hit anything with cleaner yet.<P>Are there any thermal breakin procedures I should follow like when breaking in a new rotor?||||reg||1
